    escalation: 'Los atributos de RRHH no llegan al usuario (el feed HR→AD/Entra no existe o es incompleto): proyecto aparte — sin fuente de datos confiable no hay automatización; escalar al dueño del HRIS con la lista de atributos requeridos. Casos que el workflow no cubre (contractors, reingresos complejos, accesos heredados): el proceso de excepción con dueño — y el backlog de "qué automate después" lo prioriza el líder de IAM. Runs fallidos por licencias/UsageLocation: coordinar con el dueño del licenciamiento (el bloqueo de la tarea es de datos, no del workflow).',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hello, the HR-driven lifecycle automation under ticket {{TICKET_ID}} is live. Joiner and leaver workflows now trigger automatically from the HR attributes on each user (hire date and leave date): new employees receive their temporary access pass, base groups and license before day one, and departing employees are disabled with all sessions revoked at the leave date/time recorded by HR — no ticket required. Weekly monitoring of workflow runs is in place, and the standard/complex perimeter (native workflows vs. IGA-managed access) is documented with each exception owned.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Entra Lifecycle Workflows deployed at {{TIMESTAMP}} for tenant {{TENANT}}: HR attribute reliability verified first (EmployeeId/EmployeeHireDate/EmployeeLeaveDateTime per user via Get-MgUser), joiner workflow configured with time-based trigger (7 days before hire date) and task sequence (TAP generation, welcome email, birthright groups, license assignment), and leaver workflow with the full revocation chain (disable, revoke sessions, remove from groups/PIM, license retirement after mailbox conversion). Pilot validated with attribute update + run inspection (Get-MgIdentityGovernanceLifecycleWorkflowRun with per-task status), hybrid perimeter documented (native workflows for standard employee lifecycle, IGA for business roles/approvals), and weekly run-review routine established with the leaver SLA KPI (100% disabled at zero-hour) as the audit-facing metric.',
    keywords: ['lifecycle workflows', 'entra id governance', 'entra lifecycle', 'automatizacion jml', 'jml automation', 'employeehiredate', 'employeeleavedatetime', 'hr driven', 'hr-driven provisioning', 'trigger', 'workflow', 'joiner automation', 'leaver automation', 'tap', 'temporary access pass', 'runs', 'insights', 'get-mgidentitygovernancelifecycleworkflow', 'identidad gobernanza', 'onboarding automatico', 'offboarding automatico', 'sla bajas'],
