    escalation: 'Cambios de emergencia fuera del flujo (el incidente del viernes): el procedimiento de break-glass del código — cambiar, PERO el lunes el terraform plan absorbe la realidad y el PR retroactivo documenta lo que pasó. State comprometido o con sospecha: rotar las credenciales que contiene y reconstruir desde los recursos (el plan marca el camino) — escalar a security. Necesidad de gestionar con código lo que el provider no cubre (feature gap): evaluar provider REST/azapi antes de la custom solution — y documentar la excepción si toca quedarse en manual.',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hello, the IAM-as-code rollout under ticket {{TICKET_ID}} is complete for the initial scope. Access groups and their ownership are now defined as versioned Terraform code: every change goes through a pull request with a readable plan diff, peer review, and approval before apply, the state is protected in a remote backend with restricted access, drift is detected on every plan (manual portal changes are surfaced and resolved with a recorded decision), and legacy resources were adopted via import without recreation. The perimeter (Terraform for identity structure, IGA for day-to-day access) is documented.',
