    escalation: 'Combinación tóxica con USO ACTIVO (la credencial sin uso que de pronto se usa, el acceso externo nuevo que se consume): se trata como posible compromiso — caso inmediato a SOC con la evidencia de los pasos 1-4 y contención en paralelo, no remediación programada. La decisión de herramienta CIEM dedicada (volumen, multi-cloud, automatización) es del arquitecto cloud con la matriz de hallazgos como insumo.',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hello, the cloud entitlements (CIEM) assessment under ticket {{TICKET_ID}} is complete for your AWS and Azure estates. We exported a full entitlement inventory (identities, policies, and role assignments), analyzed real credential usage against the 90-day threshold, reviewed Access Analyzer findings for unintended external access, and identified toxic permission combinations across clouds. Remediation was applied per finding (unused access keys deactivated, stale Owner assignments removed, policies right-sized toward least privilege) and verified with a re-scan. A recurring governance routine is now in place: monthly entitlement diff, Access Analyzer monitoring, and scheduled access reviews for cloud roles.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'CIEM assessment executed at {{TIMESTAMP}} across AWS and Azure: full AWS entitlement baseline captured with aws iam get-account-authorization-details (users, groups, roles, inline and managed policies); credential usage analyzed from aws iam get-credential-report (password_last_used, access_key_last_used_date, 90-day threshold); Access Analyzer enumerations and findings reviewed (aws accessanalyzer list-analyzers / list-findings, external and unused access per resource policy). Azure side: full RBAC export with Get-AzRoleAssignment -Scope "/" -IncludeClassicAdministrators, plus inactive account detection via Get-MgUser SignInActivity (LastSignInDateTime older than 90 days). Toxic combination catalog applied to the cross-cloud inventory (cross-cloud admin: Azure Owner + AWS admin; public storage access + write permissions; unused service account with admin policy; exposed credential + data permissions), each finding scored by severity and usage evidence. Remediation: least-privilege right-sizing per RB-IAM-051, JIT conversion (PIM / Identity Center per RB-IAM-047/053), unused credentials revoked reversibly (aws iam update-access-key --status Inactive, Remove-AzRoleAssignment for Owner at root scope). Post-remediation re-scan verified the final state; continuous governance enabled (Access Analyzer always on, scheduled access reviews per RB-IAM-049, versioned entitlement baseline for drift detection per RB-IAM-064).',
    keywords: ['ciem', 'cloud infrastructure entitlement management', 'entitlements', 'toxic combinations', 'combinaciones toxicas', 'unused credentials', 'credential report', 'access analyzer', 'iam get-account-authorization-details', 'least privilege', 'right sizing', 'multi-cloud', 'inactivos', 'huérfanos', 'remediar', 'jit', 'pim', 'identity center'],
