    escalation: 'Aplicaciones que rompen al entrar a Protected Users: excepción documentada con owner y fecha de revisión — NADIE sale del grupo por ticket sin análisis (la salida silenciosa es la brecha que vuelve). Hallazgo de cuenta T0 iniciando sesión en estación de usuario: posible compromiso en curso — caso inmediato a SOC (ref RB-SOC-021) con los 4624 como evidencia y contención de la cuenta en paralelo.',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hello, the Active Directory tiering model under ticket {{TICKET_ID}} has been implemented for your domain. Tier 0 was inventoried and reduced to justified members only, dedicated admin accounts per level are being adopted in waves, and the golden rule is now enforced technically: high-tier credentials are denied interactive logon on lower-tier workstations by GPO. Tier 0 credentials are protected by a stricter fine-grained password policy (16+ characters, aggressive lockout) and by the Protected Users group (adopted in waves, starting with a pilot account, with documented exceptions for legacy dependencies). Current tiering violations were hunted via sign-in event analysis and are being driven to zero.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'AD tiering implementation for {{DOMAIN}} at {{TIMESTAMP}}: Tier 0 baseline captured with Get-ADGroupMember (Domain Admins recursive, Enterprise Admins, Schema Admins) and AdminSDHolder footprint via Get-ADUser -Filter AdminCount -eq 1 (includes stale protected accounts). Model documented (T0 = identity/DC/PKI-ADCS/hypervisors hosting DCs; T1 = servers/apps; T2 = workstations/helpdesk; rule: level-N credentials only log on to level ≤ N assets). Structure created (New-ADOrganizationalUnit "Tier 0", New-ADGroup Tier0-Admins). Logon restriction GPO linked to workstation OUs (Deny log on locally = Tier0-Admins, Tier1-Admins, verified with gpresult). Credential hardening: New-ADFineGrainedPasswordPolicy PSO-Tier0 (Precedence 10, MinPasswordLength 16, LockoutThreshold 3, 15-min observation window, 30-min duration, complexity enabled) applied with Add-ADFineGrainedPasswordPolicySubject; Protected Users membership adopted wave by wave starting with a single pilot account (breaks NTLM, unconstrained Kerberos delegation and CredSSP — exceptions documented with owner and review date). Violation hunting: SecurityEvent 4624 KQL summarizing admin logons by Computer/TargetUserName/LogonTypeName, driving violations to zero over 30 days; dedicated admin accounts (adm-/t0- naming) rolled out in waves with separation from browsing identities.',
    keywords: ['tiering model', 'tier 0', 'tier 1', 'tier 2', 'modelo de administracion por niveles', 'adminsdholder', 'admincount', 'domain admins', 'enterprise admins', 'protected users', 'fgpp', 'pso', 'fine grained password policy', 'new-adfinegrainedpasswordpolicy', 'escalation path', 'cuenta admin dedicada', 'separacion de credenciales', 'denegar inicio de sesion', 'defensa en profundidad'],
